      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=⟨3{e}^{t-5},\\,\\sqrt{t+4},\\,(t-3)^{4}⟩$ at $t=5?$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=5$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5) & =⟨3{e}^{5-5},\\sqrt{5+4},(5-3)^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{0},\\sqrt{9},{2}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3,16⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=5$ is the vector $⟨3,3,16⟩.$",
