    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-75003",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "Find $|r(4)|$ given that $r(t)=⟨\\frac{10}{t+1},\\,2t-2,\\,t-1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =⟨\\frac{10}{4+1},\\,2(4)-2,\\,4-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,6,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(6)}^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "5"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\sqrt{10}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2\\sqrt{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2\\sqrt{7}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "7"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "7"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-75003",
        "kp_title": "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function",
        "kp_href": null
      }
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-348688",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{t+3}⟩,$ what is $|r(0)|?$\n\n$|r(0)|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0),\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0),\\,\\sqrt{0+3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(0)| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+1+3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
