      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "Find $|r(2)|$ given that $r(t)=⟨t+1,\\,\\sqrt{t+1},\\,t⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨2+1,\\,\\sqrt{2+1},\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(2)| & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+3+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
